# AppImage — single image pipeline

Always render images through `@/components/AppImage`:

```tsx
import { AppImage, AppImageBackground } from "@/components/AppImage";

<AppImage source={Images.icon} style={styles.icon} resizeMode="contain" />
<AppImage source={{ uri: remoteUrl }} style={styles.thumb} resizeMode="cover" />

<AppImageBackground source={Images.popupBg} style={styles.bg} resizeMode="cover">
  {children}
</AppImageBackground>
```

Do **not** use `Image` or `ImageBackground` from `react-native` for UI (except inside `AppImage.tsx`).

Remote cached thumbnails: `CachedRemoteImage` from the same module (or `AppImage` with `{ uri }`).

`react-native` `Image` is only allowed for non-UI APIs: `Image.resolveAssetSource`, `Image.getSize`, etc.

Why: Bundled PNG/WebP use FastImage (reliable decode for icons and art). Icons with `tintColor` auto-route to RN Image. Remote URLs use FastImage. Local `file://` / `content://` / `ph://` use RN Image.
